// src/gen/gen.zen
// Code generation: the end of the pipeline.
//
// This file is the module's public surface and nothing else — a folder
// root is a file of starred re-exports, which is what makes a folder
// work. A name absent from this list is module-private on purpose.
//
// THE SPLIT, and it is the one STYLE.md names as its own example of
// splitting by subject: `gen` is BACKEND-SHARED PLUMBING and `gen_c` is
// THE C BACKEND. Three things are shared and none of them names C —
// where the bytes go and in what order (`gen_emit`), what a name is in
// a flat target namespace (`gen_name`), and what a backend says when it
// cannot lower something (`gen_diag`). Everything that knows what a C
// struct looks like is in `gen_c` and nowhere else. PLAN.md says a
// second backend is not to be built; keeping the seam honest costs
// nothing today and is the difference between adding one later and
// rewriting this one.
//
// DETERMINISM IS DESIGNED IN, NOT CHECKED FOR. Same input, byte-identical
// output — across repeated runs, separate processes, different absolute
// roots and shuffled input order. Three mechanisms, all of them here:
//
//   - `Emit` is the only way a byte leaves this folder, and `order` is
//     the only way a collection is put in an order. Nothing iterates a
//     `Map`; every list is sorted by a key that is a pure function of
//     the thing.
//   - A symbol is `tcode`, a pure function of the TYPE — never of a
//     counter, never of which module asked first.
//   - A `Span` carries a file relative to the compilation root, so two
//     checkouts of one tree emit the same bytes.
//
// THE ONLY `Err` IS `AllocError`. A form the backend cannot lower is a
// `Diag` collected in a `Vec`, exactly as sema's are: a program the
// backend half understands still emits the C it could, and the caller
// decides whether that is a translation unit or a report.

// where the bytes go, and the one ordering primitive
Emit*, order*, INDENT*                   = gen.gen_emit

// what a name is when the target has one flat namespace
USR*, GEN*, RES_PATH*                    = gen.gen_name
comp*, count*, path*, path_with*, segments* = gen.gen_name
sym_type*, sym_fn*, sym_variant*         = gen.gen_name
sym_member*, sym_local*, sym_value*, sym_gen* = gen.gen_name
tcode*, module_of*, res_arity*, is_failure*   = gen.gen_name

// what a backend says when it cannot lower something
GenFault*, Diag*, message*, detail*      = gen.gen_diag

// THE C BACKEND
CBackend*, emit_program*, ctype*         = gen.gen_c
